  "conclusion": "the exact (anisotropic) transform is right: it reproduces the analytic Bessel eigenvalue of a 2-D ring to < 1e-7 for both polarizations, Tidy3D's +/-R mean bend shift in 3-D to within 2 % at r_ref and 7.5 um (three cross-sections), and the cylindrical Meep resonance within the extrapolation range. femwell's isotropic eps(1+x/R)^2 overestimates the bend shift (x3.7 at R = 7.5 um; the excess scales as 1/R^2), because it approximates the conformal coordinate ln(r/R) by x/R and drops the mu tensor. modes.py uses the exact transform."
